{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004063-changing-praxes","id":1004063,"title":"Changing Praxes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-16T12:44:03-08:00","id":1004063,"title":"Changing Praxes","content":"I've combed through the book and have found almost nothing on if it's possible to change your Praxis spells, barring having a Legacy Attainment be modeled off one when you learn and gaining a Beat for it. Does anyone know something about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:51:16-08:00","id":1004067,"title":"","content":"You can buy new praxes for one arcane experience and you get a new one for each additional dot of gnosis. Are you asking if it's possible to forget a praxis spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:18:27-08:00","id":1004082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004063-changing-praxes?p=1004067#post1004067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can buy new praxes for one arcane experience and you get a new one for each additional dot of gnosis. Are you asking if it's possible to forget a praxis spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So far as I saw it, I had thought you were limited to a number of Praxes equivalent to your Gnosis, and you could not have any more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:21:15-08:00","id":1004085,"title":"","content":"You're not limited in the number of Praxes you can have, you're just limited in the number you get for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:23:21-08:00","id":1004086,"title":"","content":"On the top right of pg 112, it specifies that mages have one free praxis per dot of gnosis but may buy additional ones for one Arcane Experience each. This is corroborated by the table in the Experiences section on pg 83 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt